cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "web-search-helper: search a private corpus from a website with PHP only"
message: >-
  If you use this software in a publication, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Warith
    family-names: HARCHAOUI
    email: warithmetics@deraison.ai
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3487-7134"
    affiliation: "Deraison AI"
repository-code: "https://github.com/warith-harchaoui/web-search-helper"
url: "https://github.com/warith-harchaoui/web-search-helper"
abstract: >-
  web-search-helper indexes a corpus on the author's machine (passages cut
  into model-sized windows, sentence-transformers embeddings, a BM25 lexical
  index, section centroids) and serves it from a single PHP endpoint, while
  the visitor's question is embedded in the browser with transformers.js.
  The corpus is never published: the endpoint returns short excerpts of the
  passages that answer, or nothing when a measured rule says the corpus does
  not treat the question. A Python twin of the PHP engine calibrates the
  thresholds and is checked against it.
keywords:
  - semantic search
  - BM25
  - hybrid search
  - PHP
  - transformers.js
  - abstention
